 "notes": "Chart Nine, pages 118-119. Page 118 (left) is entirely printed annotation text plus page number; the ledger grid is on page 119 (right) only. Rows with no handwritten entries (10, SAT.11, 13, 14, 15, 20, 21, 23, 24, SAT.25, 27, 28, 29, APR.SAT.1, 3, 5, 10, 12, 13, 14, 17, 18, 19) are omitted per instructions. April 7 (Friday, Good Friday 1939) has no row at all between rows \"6\" and \"SAT.8\", consistent with a market holiday. Two checksum discrepancies were found and flagged uncertain rather than force-fit: row dated March 22 (KP off by 1 point from literal US+BS) and row dated March 30 (BS cell of uncertain column/value, causing KP to be 3/4 point off from literal US+BS). All other rows with complete US/BS/KP triads checksum exactly. Ink-color convention (UT=black, DT=red, SR/NR/NRC/SRC=blue) was used to cross-check column assignments throughout, per instructions.",
